Here is the assembly language version of BinHex, a program to convert Mac
resource/data files into mailable .Hex files and back.  It is much faster
than the BASIC version, can handle files with both data and resource forks,
and can produce/decode "compressed" files (ASCII rather than hex coding).

This version of BinHex is itself encoded in .Hex format.  Use the BASIC
version to convert it to BinHex.Tmp, then use BinHex.Tmp to convert this
file to BinHex, then throw away BinHex.Bas, BinHex.Hex, and BinHex.Tmp.

